{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3454","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3454","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3454\",\"parent_revision\":\"8c53083b0395099ea3bde3a106e204e253353553\",\"root_revision\":\"1fe1c9a481db35b8718f25f82a7163f8b2f0cb6e64d67c47a610443df9c66c10\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-09-06\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`hooks/session-start-session-id.cjs` captures `session_id` at SessionStart and is meant to make it available to later Bash tool calls. Observed on a real wave: it delivered nothing, and every worker degraded through the same three-step ladder.\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA worker instructed to identify its session cannot, and improvises. Downstream, anything keyed on that value lands somewhere unattributable, and no error is raised at any point in the chain.\\n\\n**Hypothesis**: the 2026-08-28 run hit one of the three early-exit branches. Not confirmed \u2014 the branch taken was not captured, and the run is not reproducible from the transcripts alone.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session audit of the SubagentStop correlation path, 2026-09-06\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-09-06\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Observed\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAcross 26 `active-task set` tool calls in the sub-agent transcripts of one wave dated 2026-08-28, each worker issued the documented form first, then a shell default, then a hardcoded label:\\n\\n| Worker | 1st attempt | 2nd | 3rd |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| performance-worker | `\\\"${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}\\\"` | `\\\"${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID:-performance-worker-session}\\\"` | `performance-worker` |\\n| qg-t6-contextrefine | `\\\"${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}\\\"` | `\\\"${\u2026:-qg-t6-contextrefine}\\\"` | `qg-t6-contextrefine` |\\n| qg-t5-docupdate | `\\\"${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}\\\"` | `\\\"${\u2026:-unknown}\\\"` | `qg-t5-doc-update` |\\n| t4-3277 | `\\\"${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}\\\"` | `\\\"${\u2026:-t4-3277}\\\"` | \u2014 |\\n\\nEvery worker followed the instruction as written before degrading. The escalation is the signature of an unset variable, not of an agent going off-script.\\n\\nThat session's own transcript contains zero injected `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=<uuid>` context lines and zero mentions of `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE`.\\n\\nThe hook predates those runs: added 2026-04-06 in `05be9718a`.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Residue On Disk\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n`~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/` currently holds records keyed `unknown`, `performance-worker`, `qg-T1-code-review-3169`, `security-worker-session`, and literally `active-task-${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}.json` \u2014 the unexpanded string, reaching a writer that never saw a shell.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n`~/.dh/projects/{slug}/context/` currently holds records keyed `unknown`, `performance-worker`, `qg-T1-code-review-3169`, `security-worker-session`, and literally `active-task-${CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID}.json` \u2014 the unexpanded string, reaching a writer that never saw a shell.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Where The Hook Stops Early\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\n`session-start-session-id.cjs` returns `{}` without writing in three cases: `process.env.CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` already set (`:31-34`), stdin not parseable as JSON (`:38-43`), and `session_id` missing or non-string (`:46-49`). It writes to the env file only when `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE` is set and does not already contain the variable (`:53-63`). No branch reports that it declined.\\n\\nThe first of those fires in a nested session. This machine's environment carries `CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION=1` alongside a populated `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`, which is the shape that guard is written for \u2014 and in that case the inherited value belongs to an outer session rather than the current one.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\n`session-start-session-id.cjs` returns `{}` without writing in three cases: `process.env.CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` already set (`:31-34`), stdin not parseable as JSON (`:38-43`), and `session_id` missing or non-string (`:46-49`). It writes to the env file only when `CLAUDE_ENV_FILE` is set and does not already contain the variable (`:53-63`). No branch reports that it declined.\\n\\nThe first of those fires in a nested session. This machine's environment carries `CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION=1` alongside a populated `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`, which is the shape that guard is written for \u2014 and in that case the inherited value belongs to an outer session rather than the current one.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Scope Note\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-0</sub>\\n\\nIndependent of whether the active-task record survives. The variable is injected for general use and is also read by the kage-bunshin hooks; the delivery defect stands regardless of what consumes the value.\\n</div>\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z-1</sub>\\n\\nIndependent of whether the active-task record survives. The variable is injected for general use and is also read by the kage-bunshin hooks; the delivery defect stands regardless of what consumes the value.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"0dbb8bdcc400c35a13931d1f6ef9e9a3fde358cf75f9e3cb01db210fb7cf75e6\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABUIyUqA\"}"}